["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ark", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Archival Resource Key (ARK)](https://arks.org/about/), is a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) suited to being a persistent identifier for information objects of any type, standardized by the [ARK Identifier Scheme](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-kunze-ark/) Internet-Draft. It consists of the \"ark:\" label followed by a Name Assigning Authority Number, a forward slash, a name, and an optional qualifier (e.g., `ark:12148/btv1b8449691v/f29`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/ExpandedLicensing/License", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Abstract class for the portion of an AnyLicenseInfo representing a license.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/issn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Serial Number (ISSN)](https://www.issn.org/understanding-the-issn/what-is-an-issn/) is an eight-digit identifier for serial publications and other continuing resources standardized by [ISO 3297](https://www.iso.org/standard/84536.html). It consists of two groups of four digits separated by a hyphen, where the final character is a check digit that may be an \"X\". The hyphen is retained when the identifier is stored electronically to maintain the standard 9-character string format (e.g., `1464-3693`). The ISSN is media-specific; the same journal title may be assigned different identifiers for its physical and digital versions.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/AI/informationAboutApplication", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Information about the AI software, not including the model description.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "System Package Data Exchange\u2122 (SPDX\u00ae) Ontology", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/contentIdentifier", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/ContentIdentifier", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/secureSoftwareAttestation", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to information assuring that the software is developed using security practices as defined by [NIST SP 800-218 Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final) or [CISA Secure Software Development Attestation Form](https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-software-development-attestation-form).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/nli", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType", "globalId", "", ""]
